Z||000002||2xsess||01-21-2001||12:29 PM||||I was thinking of starting a thread similar to this one to see if anyone has my old 88GT t-top, I traded it in Coconut Creek FL at Tom Hendricks Toyota, it was black but the windshield pilar was still red. It didn't have the 88 specific wheels on it. Gray Gt Lace wheels,5 spd. Gray interior, the drivers seat was in excellent shape, no tears. Can't think of anything else right now. <P>Anyone know if there's a way to find it with the VIN, I haven't found the VIN yet but I might be able to dig it up. I just want to know if it's still out there on the road.<BR><P>------------------<BR>Jeff<BR>AOL IM : Only2xsess<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/My_car_(large)sig_1.JPG">   <BR> <A HREF="http://kresgeus.homestead.com/FieroPage.html" TARGET=_blank>http://kresgeus.homestead.com/FieroPage.html</A> ||||reg||1
Z||000003||ur2biteme||01-22-2001||04:04 AM||||well, this will bump this topic back up at least, but i guess i'm in the same boat.  <P>way back in '88 (lol) my mom was working for WQLT in Flourence, AL. and as part of a promotion, got the opportunity to demo a car of her choice from the pontiac dealer.  it was a red '88 base coupe, sunroof, auto, pw, pl, pm, ac, am/fm cassette, and sunroof (trying to remember if it had a luggage rack, bear with me, i was 9 or 10 at the time).  i think that was all the options, could be wrong.  anyways, she wound up buying it.  part of the divorce stuff included having to declare bankrupcy, and she wound up moving out here later that same year to take a better job.  anyway, that particular dealer was adamant about getting the car back after she signed the dotted line, and took the opportunity of her being 2 weeks late on payment to find her and repo it.  (as far as i know, it was an illegal repo because she DID NOT default on the car) this would have been late '89, early '90.  she had also moved cross-country in it (obviously she didnt take much) so it would have been registered in AL originally, then changed to CA in late '88 i believe.  i would love to know what happened to it just for grins, and if the price is right.......    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>wish i had more info on the car.  i just hope it didnt wind up in a crusher.  i keep seeing red 88 coupes and it peaks my curiosity.  <P>------------------<BR>Bob's '87 econo coupe<BR>170k awaiting a tranny <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"><BR> <A HREF="http://members.fortunecity.com/ur2biteme" TARGET=_blank>http://members.fortunecity.com/ur2biteme</A> <p>[This message has been edited by ur2biteme (edited 01-22-2001).]||||reg||1
